X:301
T:Skeppare Schottische
M:4/4
N:"the Skipper". Said to have been made by Thöre Härdelin to mark the occasion of his boat sinking in Stockholm harbour.
N:I've picked this up in sessions around England, and I suspect it's become somewhat folk-processed -
N:I'm not sure I've ever heard played straight as a schottis.
O:Sweden
R:Schottis
Z:Richard Robinson <URL:http://www.qualmograph.org.uk/contact.html>
